# Forward Architecture Cutoff (July 2026)

**Parent strategy** for PasteCraft structure. **Implementation detail:** `vertical-slice-modularity.mdc`. **Full spec:** [docs/architecture/FORWARD-ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/architecture/FORWARD-ARCHITECTURE.md).

## Cutoff

From **2026-07-05**, new or materially changed code follows **Modular Vertical Slices + Legacy Facades** — no big-bang rewrite.

## Legacy vs new (path convention)

| New (forward) | Legacy (do not add logic) |
|---|---|
| `extension/content/<feature>/` | `extension/popup.js`, `quick-paste/quick-paste.js` |
| `extension/popup/features/<feature>/` | Root shims until facaded |
| `extension/background/handlers/`, `messaging/` | Pre-cutoff ad-hoc roots |
| `extension/supabase/*.js` | |
| **`extension/bridges/<domain>/`** — ACL to legacy | |

No `extension/legacy/` mass move. Optional header: `@forward-slice` / `@legacy-cutoff`.

## Bridge rules

1. Slices **never** import legacy monoliths directly — use **one facade per domain** in `extension/bridges/<domain>/`.
2. Facade owns ID normalization, sync queue, storage quirks.
3. Cross-context: `message-types.js` + router — not ad-hoc message strings.
4. **Extract on touch:** facade first → extract to slice → shrink legacy.

## Forbidden

- New business logic in monolith files.
- Cross-slice imports (use shared API, messages, storage keys).
- Mass file moves without explicit migration ticket.
- Auto-refactor without explicit migration intent (Arkitect policy).

## Before structural work

Run Arkitect: `diagnose_repository` → `recommend_patterns` → (if legacy) `analyze_refactoring_opportunities`. See FORWARD-ARCHITECTURE.md §10.

## Agent default

Implement on `main` until SUCCESS → task branch commit. CodeScene on changed files. Ask Ezequiel before SuccessLog.
